==== Backup Firmware ====

See: [[toh:t-com:spw701v#backing_up_original_firmware|SpeedportW701V]] and [[toh:avm:fritz.box.wlan.7112#backup_firmware|FRITZ!Box Fon WLAN 7112]].

=== Serial & TFTP ===
  * get a TFTP Server, e.g. [[https://code.google.com/archive/p/tftpgui/|tftpgui]] [[https://storage.googleapis.com/google-code-archive-downloads/v2/code.google.com/tftpgui/tftpgui_2_2.tar|version 2.2]] - [[https://storage.googleapis.com/google-code-archive-downloads/v2/code.google.com/tftpgui/tftpgui_3_1.tar|version 3.1]] (did not work on Ubuntu 16.10, April2017) and required packages: ''sudo apt-get install python python-tk''
  * set PC-Lan-IP to: 192.168.178.3, Sub: 255.255.255.0, Gateway: 192.168.178.1
  * start tftpgui: ''sudo python tftpgui.py''
  * start serial terminal, e.g.: ''sudo screen /dev/ttyUSB0 115200''
  * power on FRITZ!Box and wait till boot finished
  * press Enter to activate BusyBox console:\\ <code>
cat /proc/mtd
cat /dev/mtdblock0 | tftp -p -l - -r rootfs.image 192.168.178.3
cat /dev/mtdblock1 | tftp -p -l - -r kernel.image 192.168.178.3
cat /dev/mtdblock2 | tftp -p -l - -r urlader.image 192.168.178.3
cat /dev/mtdblock3 | tftp -p -l - -r tffs1.image 192.168.178.3
cat /dev/mtdblock4 | tftp -p -l - -r tffs2.image 192.168.178.3
cat /dev/mtdblock5 | tftp -p -l - -r jffs2.image 192.168.178.3
cat /dev/mtdblock6 | tftp -p -l - -r mtd_nor.image 192.168.178.3
</code>
  * images should be in ../tftpgui/tftproot

==== Flash Firmware ====

=== Web Interface ===
Flashing via the Webinterface is not working at the moment. (march 2021)

Default IP: 192.168.178.1 (OEM Firmware), 192.168.1.1 (LEDE, OpenWrt)

Emergency OEM IP: Box is always available on http://169.254.1.1. Set PC IP-address manually in range of 169.254.1.x
If a default password is set try: 0000

=== FTP ===
Flashing a non fitting image causes Box not to boot. Flashing back [[#Backup Firmware|firmware_backup]] or [[#debricking|stock_kernel.image]] via FTP helps.

OpenWrt can be installed via the EVA bootloader. The EVA bootloader waits in the first 5 seconds after power-on for an FTP connection on 192.168.178.1. Set your IP address to 192.168.178.2 and upload the image like following. 

<code>
ftp -n -4 192.168.178.1

  ftp> quote USER adam2
  ftp> quote PASS adam2
  ftp> binary
  ftp> debug
  ftp> passive
  ftp> quote MEDIA FLSH
  ftp> put openwrt-sysupgrade.bin mtd1
  ftp> quote REBOOT
  ftp> quit
</code>
Important: while flashing wait for ftp promt showing up again or watch in serial terminal: erase mtd1 .... flash .....

Power on happens around five seconds after plugging in the power supply. All LEDs flash once. ping 192.168.178.1 can help to see this time window.
If this time window is not available for some reason, it is also possible to interrupt boot by immediately pressing a key in serial terminal and then start the FTP connection.

(optional) erase configuration partition mtd3 & mtd4 -> default FTP-IP address (192.168.178.1) can change to 192.168.2.1
<code>
erase mtd3
erase mtd4
restart
</code>

Flashing Bootloader not tested & recommended (watch out for mtd2).

===== Debricking =====

-> get [[https://download.avm.de/fritz.box/|stock firmware]] -> rename it to .tar -> find and extract kernel.image -> [[#flash firmware|flash kernel.image]]

-> bootloop of a faulty device -> [[http://freetz.org/|build]] a minimal firmware.image:
  * make menuconfig
  * check everything @ "Removal patches" except "Remove WLAN"
  * @ "Other patches" disable all "AVM daemons"
  * rename firmware.image to .tar -> find and extract kernel.image -> [[#flash firmware|flash kernel.image]]

-> [[docs:guide-user:troubleshooting:generic.debrick]]


